   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to creating annual\nreporting obligations by municipal housing authorities to the authorities\nbudget office with respect to state-funded activities of such municipal\nhousing authorities",
    "basePrintNo": "S3156",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3156-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2801, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3156A\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to creating\nannual reporting obligations by municipal housing authorities to the\nauthorities budget office with respect to state-funded activities of\nsuch municipal housing authorities\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill ensures that municipal housing authorities report budget and\ncapital information on state funded activities annually to the Authori-\nties Budget Office.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nRequires that municipal housing authorities report budget and capital\ninformation on state funded activities annually to the Authorities Budg-\net Office.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe bill would strengthen the Public Authorities Reform Act by requiring\nthat municipal housing authorities report budget and capital information\non state funded activities annually to the Authorities Budget Office.\nMunicipal Housing Authorities are unique entities that have oversight at\nthe Federal, State and City level; this bill works to find a compromise\npoint where the ABO may have appropriate oversight on these important\nentities.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSimilar Bills--S. 7913 of 2018, A. 10279 of 2018\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
